direct-to-backend health check: 200
direct-to-backend, no X-Access-Channel header at all: 200 (defaults to intranet per middleware.py line 84)

[PASS] backend accepts a client-supplied X-Access-Channel: intranet header with no way to verify it came from nginx -- confirms the trust boundary is nginx's proxy_set_header alone -- if the backend port is ever reachable without going through nginx (misconfigured network, debug port, container escape), any caller can claim to be on the intranet channel unconditionally

This is an accepted infra-trust boundary, not something this test 'fixes' -- see the plan's CONF-03 note. The mitigation is deployment-level: never expose the api container's port to anything but nginx (docker-compose.yml already does this correctly via `expose:` not `ports:`).

